## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 2 (systemic — affects 10/10 tests) |
| **Medium** | 1 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method is called, giving you 95%+ line coverage, but almost nothing is actually *verified*. Bugs ship because these tests cannot fail when behavior regresses.

---

### 🔴 Critical #1 — No Assertions (5 tests)

**Affected:** `AddProduct_Works` (L17), `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33), `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39), `GetProductCount_Works` (L64), `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L69), `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85)

These methods execute code and return — that's it. They can never fail unless an exception is thrown.

**Fix examples:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    Assert.AreEqual(product, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}

[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnretrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}

[TestMethod]
public void ApplyBulkDiscount_ReducesPricesByFraction()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 10.00m));
    _catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.00m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ImportFromCsv_ParsesAndStoresProduct()
{
    _catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
    var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.IsNotNull(product);
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
}
```

---

### 🔴 Critical #2 — Trivial `IsNotNull` Masquerading as Verification (4 tests)

**Affected:** `GetProduct_Works` (L28), `SearchProducts_Works` (L51), `GetAllProducts_Works` (L59), `ExportToCsv_Works` (L81)

`Assert.IsNotNull` proves only that the method returned *something*. It doesn't verify correctness. `Search("Widget")` could return `["Gadget"]` and this test passes.

**Fix examples:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetProduct_ReturnsMatchingProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result!.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void Search_ReturnsOnlyMatchingProducts()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
    var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
    Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ExportToCsv_FormatsCorrectly()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99));
    var csv = _catalog.ExportToCsv();
    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001,Widget,9.99", csv);
}
```

